(1216191, 151501, 21330, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EaThis:</b></div><hr/><i> The red is way harsh to be a "light" color, but it''s a great shot. Could have been just a little more room above the scoop to get more symmetry to the shot. 6 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks you''ve summarised what the consensus for what I did wrong in this shot.  <br/>1. Too bright for light, perhaps leaving off the topping would''ve been better  <br/>2. My cropping was too tight, this unfortunatly was due to the prop (plate) I had very distracting pattern around the rim which I felt confused the image so I... Lesson: Get good props :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by EaThis: The red is way harsh to be a "light" color, but it''s a great shot. Could have been just a little more room above the scoop to get more symmetry to the shot. 6   Thanks you''ve summarised what the consensus for what I did wrong in this shot.  1. Too bright for light, perhaps leaving off the topping would''ve been better  2. My cropping was too tight, this unfortunatly was due to the prop (plate) I had very distracting pattern around the rim which I felt confused the image so I... Lesson: Get good props :-)', '2005-03-09 00:19:41.000000', NULL, 0),
