(1219101, 150763, 6912, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by menardmam:</b></div><hr/><i> Can you comment/tell how you have done that (infrared filter ?) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I used normal studio lighting with no filters, the girl was very blond and with fair skin, I used some close to white make up, white lipstick and white mascara also. Her hair was sprayed with some ice spray. The original photo was close to light itself. then I turned it into monotoe, duotone with a light tint of blue. sRGB+sharpen. I think a good thing for this photo was that I used a hair spot from the right top corner and it shines through her hair to make them look lighter. <br/>thank you everyone for such nice comments, the girl is a real beauty, i think I will do more things with her in the future.</td>', 'Originally posted by menardmam: Can you comment/tell how you have done that (infrared filter ?)  I used normal studio lighting with no filters, the girl was very blond and with fair skin, I used some close to white make up, white lipstick and white mascara also. Her hair was sprayed with some ice spray. The original photo was close to light itself. then I turned it into monotoe, duotone with a light tint of blue. sRGB+sharpen. I think a good thing for this photo was that I used a hair spot from the right top corner and it shines through her hair to make them look lighter. thank you everyone for such nice comments, the girl is a real beauty, i think I will do more things with her in the future.', '2005-03-10 01:47:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(1219113, 150976, 17613, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a worthy winner. It never fails to surprise me (and you would think I should have learnt by now) that quite often the simplest of ideas wins. This is not an attempt to take the glory from this image by the way. <br/> <br/>On occasions one sees fantastic images, with a vast amount of preparation before the shot is taken, then a fair amount of post editing, which is all the result of vivid imagination and thought. I admire the work produced by these people. <br/> <br/>Then one of these hits you, so simple, so beautiful, and you think to yourself "WHY THE HELL DIDN''T I THINK OF THAT" Well done arngrimur.<br/> <br/>Now I will go away and sulk.</td>', 'Congratulations on a worthy winner. It never fails to surprise me (and you would think I should have learnt by now) that quite often the simplest of ideas wins. This is not an attempt to take the glory from this image by the way.  On occasions one sees fantastic images, with a vast amount of preparation before the shot is taken, then a fair amount of post editing, which is all the result of vivid imagination and thought. I admire the work produced by these people.  Then one of these hits you, so simple, so beautiful, and you think to yourself "WHY THE HELL DIDN''T I THINK OF THAT" Well done arngrimur. Now I will go away and sulk.', '2005-03-10 02:01:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1219133, 151681, 34746, '<td valign="top">Superb! Congrats!</td>', 'Superb! Congrats!', '2005-03-10 03:14:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1219221, 151707, 15832, '<td valign="top">Hi Christoph.<br/>This is a really creative entry and the setup an cropping is working good in this case...  What you could maby have done better is...<br/>Clean the CD and have the focus on him. Like you can see,  the CD is not too focused and littel dirty (spots on it). Than you should have tried to do it in WB (whitebalance (filter)) I think the snow would become whiter if you would have done that....<br/>I wonder if you used flash?<br/>Nice take on the challenge...  You just have to keep on and on... <br/>Thats how you learn;)<br/>Heard you got 5,8 in the momment for your entry in surrealism!!<br/>That is a very good grade!!!  Some peopel here never got that high!!!<br/>Good luck...   asij<br/></td>', 'Hi Christoph.This is a really creative entry and the setup an cropping is working good in this case...  What you could maby have done better is...Clean the CD and have the focus on him. Like you can see,  the CD is not too focused and littel dirty (spots on it). Than you should have tried to do it in WB (whitebalance (filter)) I think the snow would become whiter if you would have done that....I wonder if you used flash?Nice take on the challenge...  You just have to keep on and on... Thats how you learn;)Heard you got 5,8 in the momment for your entry in surrealism!!That is a very good grade!!!  Some peopel here never got that high!!!Good luck...   asij', '2005-03-10 06:05:27.000000', NULL, 0),
