(1454738, 151494, 15711, '<td valign="top">Staged but nice. I like the off center of the gems and the softer focus.  Would make a great beginning to a window display.</td>', 'Staged but nice. I like the off center of the gems and the softer focus.  Would make a great beginning to a window display.', '2005-06-14 12:40:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476645, 151296, 14986, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.  It reminds me of one I took here last winter.  We had a snowstorm and I passed one of those plastic lightup nativity scenes where all the figures were buried up to their necks in snow, and the poor baby Jesus was no place to be seen!  LOL  It really was funny.<br/> <br/>Anyway, I think this fit the challenge well and I think you chose a difficult thing to photograph - snow.  It does seem really blown out in the center and the blue tint is a little strong in places.  I do like the idea, however.</td>', 'Nice idea.  It reminds me of one I took here last winter.  We had a snowstorm and I passed one of those plastic lightup nativity scenes where all the figures were buried up to their necks in snow, and the poor baby Jesus was no place to be seen!  LOL  It really was funny. Anyway, I think this fit the challenge well and I think you chose a difficult thing to photograph - snow.  It does seem really blown out in the center and the blue tint is a little strong in places.  I do like the idea, however.', '2005-06-22 20:30:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1478341, 150259, 15711, '<td valign="top">Love the white on white. The eyes and nose make such a nice contrast.  Excellent!!!</td>', 'Love the white on white. The eyes and nose make such a nice contrast.  Excellent!!!', '2005-06-23 13:21:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1486515, 151341, 18028, '<td valign="top">I just discovered this image, GREAT shot.<br/> <br/>very artsy and somewhat provocative, love it.<br/> <br/>Technically very powerful use of light and miraculous use of the blinds...with no "zebra effect".<br/> <br/>constructive comment:  the only thing that "bugs" me is the shadow of the hair...perhaps some cloning out to make the hair seem more "in place".</td>', 'I just discovered this image, GREAT shot. very artsy and somewhat provocative, love it. Technically very powerful use of light and miraculous use of the blinds...with no "zebra effect". constructive comment:  the only thing that "bugs" me is the shadow of the hair...perhaps some cloning out to make the hair seem more "in place".', '2005-06-27 14:55:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1492940, 151599, 37719, '<td valign="top">I wasn''t a member when this challenge was run but I wish I was.  Perhaps I could have helped you out in the ranks.  I think a lot of people missed the boat on this one.  The hint/obviousness of being nude was a definite draw since the focal point had nothing to do with the state of undress.  I think the angle/perspective is excellent and the lighting perfect for the skin tone.  I think this would be a good leading lines shot - the nose definitely makes you scan the whole body.  I like this shot.  Probably an 8 or 9 on first round.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-29 18:48:00.</i></td>', 'I wasn''t a member when this challenge was run but I wish I was.  Perhaps I could have helped you out in the ranks.  I think a lot of people missed the boat on this one.  The hint/obviousness of being nude was a definite draw since the focal point had nothing to do with the state of undress.  I think the angle/perspective is excellent and the lighting perfect for the skin tone.  I think this would be a good leading lines shot - the nose definitely makes you scan the whole body.  I like this shot.  Probably an 8 or 9 on first round.', '2005-06-29 19:46:32.000000', '2005-06-29 19:48:00.000000', 0),
(1494226, 150381, 31772, '<td valign="top">Beautiful composition... I like the subject matter too.</td>', 'Beautiful composition... I like the subject matter too.', '2005-06-30 03:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
